1. tree command
Purpose: Displays the directory structure in a tree format.

Command:
mkdir project
cd project
mkdir docs src
touch README.txt docs/file1.txt src/main.py
tree


Expected output:
.
├── docs
│   └── file1.txt
├── README.txt
└── src
    └── main.py

3 directories, 3 files


If tree is not installed, run:
sudo apt install tree


2. head command
Purpose: Displays the first 10 lines of a file.

Create a sample log file:
for i in {1..15}; do echo "Log entry $i"; done > log.txt


Command:
head log.txt


Expected output:
Log entry 1
Log entry 2
Log entry 3
Log entry 4
Log entry 5
Log entry 6
Log entry 7
Log entry 8
Log entry 9
Log entry 10


3. tail command
Purpose: Displays the last 10 lines of a file.

Command:
tail log.txt


Expected output:
Log entry 6
Log entry 7
Log entry 8
Log entry 9
Log entry 10
Log entry 11
Log entry 12
Log entry 13
